WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.374 --> 00:00:03.342
(whooshing)
(thudding)

00:00:03.342 --> 00:00:06.092
(dramatic music)

00:00:11.838 --> 00:00:13.639
Even when I was playing
football, I'd kick the ball

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:16.283
against the wall and I'd
pretend that I scored a goal

00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:19.270
and I'd run off and I'd be raising my hand

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:22.494
and visualizing a arena full of fans.

00:00:22.494 --> 00:00:24.262
That was something I'd done as a kid

00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:27.108
out on my own, I just run around kicking

00:00:27.108 --> 00:00:27.941
the ball.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:35.677
And then I suppose when
I came to these events

00:00:35.677 --> 00:00:37.575
and started training MMA
and I came to an event,

00:00:37.575 --> 00:00:38.992
it was like okay.

00:00:41.943 --> 00:00:42.859
And then,

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:44.074
now I'm doing it.

00:00:44.074 --> 00:00:45.986
- [Interviewer] Did you
ever have, let's call it

00:00:45.986 --> 00:00:48.898
a normal job, kind of a 9-to-5?

00:00:48.898 --> 00:00:51.014
- Yeah, 'cause the Irish thing

00:00:51.014 --> 00:00:53.387
is to get into a trade
straightaway, I was no different.

00:00:53.387 --> 00:00:55.720
As soon as I finished school

00:00:58.465 --> 00:01:00.947
Doing this, doing that.

00:01:00.947 --> 00:01:02.709
They didn't know what
it was, they didn't know

00:01:02.709 --> 00:01:03.876
what MMA was,

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:06.463
As far as they were concerned,

00:01:06.463 --> 00:01:07.916
my mom and dad, I'm talking
about, as far as they

00:01:07.916 --> 00:01:09.527
were concerned, I was just
getting into a cage and fighting

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:11.714
with some other guy, they
didn't know nothing about it.

00:01:11.714 --> 00:01:12.718
No one did, really,

00:01:12.718 --> 00:01:13.911
but

00:01:13.911 --> 00:01:18.078
You know what I mean, I knew (mumbles).

00:01:18.974 --> 00:01:20.795
Because obviously I had a lot
of fights with me dad, a lot--

00:01:20.795 --> 00:01:24.045
- [Interviewer] What trade did you get?

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.996
- Were you actually in the trenches?

00:01:28.996 --> 00:01:32.559
- I mean it was an industrial
so I'd be like building this.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.543
It'd be like the plumbing that
would be needed in a place

00:01:34.543 --> 00:01:36.751
like this, six o'clock in the morning

00:01:36.751 --> 00:01:38.168
and the motorway.

00:01:40.641 --> 00:01:42.234
To get to the motorway and
then I'd stand on the edge

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.533
of the motorway and wait
for a bloke to drive by

00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:47.717
so he'd give me a lift and
then the motorway was getting

00:01:47.717 --> 00:01:49.458
renovation at times, it
would take me two hours,

00:01:49.458 --> 00:01:51.404
2 1/2 hours to get to
the place, it was out

00:01:51.404 --> 00:01:52.654
in the country.

00:01:53.768 --> 00:01:55.809
And I was the first
year, so I was the worst

00:01:55.809 --> 00:01:58.012
of the worst.
- Wow.

00:01:58.012 --> 00:02:01.316
Then two hours to get back in
the traffic again, which is

00:02:01.316 --> 00:02:03.483
a horrible, horrible time.

00:02:05.362 --> 00:02:08.862
I lasted 18 months doing it, it was tough.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.030
And then John said

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.152
'cause I was training with John
as well at the time and then

00:02:15.152 --> 00:02:18.365
John (mumbles) and says, "I
have a show, I'm doing a show.

00:02:18.365 --> 00:02:20.948
"I'd like you to fight in it."

00:02:22.333 --> 00:02:24.450
My dad used to come in and
punch the hell out of me and try

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.511
and drag me out of bed.

00:02:26.511 --> 00:02:27.886
I hadn't (mumbles)

00:02:27.886 --> 00:02:28.825
for a few good years when

00:02:28.825 --> 00:02:32.742
I'm (mumbles) and that was it.

00:02:39.224 --> 00:02:41.028
It was a lot of stressful
years, know what I mean?

00:02:41.028 --> 00:02:43.028
A lot of tough times but

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:50.699
Everything I do in my
life is related to this.

00:02:54.902 --> 00:02:56.235
And that is why, now what I mean,

00:02:56.235 --> 00:02:57.735
to be--
- Is that--

00:03:01.668 --> 00:03:02.918
- I don't know.

00:03:05.588 --> 00:03:06.963
I'm in phenomenal shape,

00:03:06.963 --> 00:03:08.943
in body and mind, to me, what's unhealthy

00:03:08.943 --> 00:03:11.346
is living an unhealthy life,
to me, what's unhealthy

00:03:11.346 --> 00:03:12.847
is getting up and going
through the same day

00:03:12.847 --> 00:03:15.387
every day of your life,
9-to-5 in an office

00:03:15.387 --> 00:03:16.220
or in a,

00:03:19.369 --> 00:03:20.452
I don't work.

00:03:25.207 --> 00:03:29.653
That's why it's become a career
for me because I love it.

00:03:29.653 --> 00:03:33.320
(ambient electronic music)

